          {
            "title": "Invalid module construction for multi-config helper",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/hexo/index.js",
            "line": 36,
            "explanation": "`require('./multi_config_path')` returns a plain function, but the new code invokes it with `new`. That creates an object instead of the callable path resolver, so `mcp(base, args.config)` later throws `TypeError: mcp is not a function` for any `--config` value.",
            "suggestion": "Call the exported factory directly: `var mcp = require('./multi_config_path')(this);` or change the module to export a constructor consistently.",
            "failureAfterChange": "Starting Hexo with `new Hexo('/site', {config: '_config.yml'})` now crashes when reading `this.config_path` because `mcp` is not callable.",
